    <description>Replaces standard Convert. No agent prompt — silently matches an existing Business Account first (QID/Phone/Email) via AF_LeadConversionService, creating one only if no match is found. Always targets the Business_Account record type explicitly (never Person Account) and creates/reuses a Brand Profile Contact for the lead&apos;s brand. Results screen uses the afLeadConvertSummary LWC (backed by AF_LeadConversionSummaryController) to render the created/linked records as real SLDS cards with standard record icons — DisplayText rich text was tried first but Salesforce&apos;s sanitizer strips border/border-radius styling, so it could never visually match the native Convert screen.

REORDERED: Screen_AssignRep (sales rep picker) now runs BEFORE any DML — Convert_Lead, Stamp_Deposit_Bypass, Update_Opportunity_Owner, and Create_Assignment_Task all happen only after the rep is selected and the screen is submitted. Previously Convert_Lead ran first and Screen_AssignRep came after, so closing the browser on that screen left a converted Lead with a real Account/Contact/Opportunity already committed and no rep ever assigned — every screen before a Screen element commits its preceding DML once Salesforce renders that screen, so nothing before the first screen the user can actually cancel out of should perform DML.

Sales rep picker also now filters to the BU-matching &quot;Sales Rep - &lt;BU&gt;&quot; role (via Get_SalesRepRole + ChoiceSet_SalesReps) instead of listing every User in the org.</description>
    <dynamicChoiceSets>
        <name>ChoiceSet_SalesReps</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <displayField>LastName</displayField>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>UserRoleId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>var_SalesRepRoleRecord.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>IsActive</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <limit>200</limit>
        <object>User</object>
        <valueField>Id</valueField>
    </dynamicChoiceSets>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>AF_Formula_ErrorDisplayMessage</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(NOT(ISBLANK({!Convert_Lead.errorMessage})), {!Convert_Lead.errorMessage}, {!$Flow.FaultMessage})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>AF_Formula_SalesRepRoleName</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>CASE({!Get_Lead.AF_BusinessUnit__c},
    &quot;Alfardan Automobiles&quot;, &quot;Sales Rep - Automobiles&quot;,
    &quot;Alfardan Premier Motors&quot;, &quot;Sales Rep - PremierMotors&quot;,
    &quot;Alfardan Sports Motors&quot;, &quot;Sales Rep - SportsMotors&quot;,
    &quot;&quot;)</expression>
    </formulas>
